<h2>⚡ Quick Snippets</h2>
<p>Version 1.2 adds <b>Quick Snippets</b> — a folder pinned to the top of your
snippets that holds up to 10 entries, each mapped to a number key.</p>
<ul>
  <li>Press <code>⇧⌘S</code> and the Quick Snippets folder opens automatically.</li>
  <li>Press <code>1</code>–<code>9</code> (or <code>0</code> for the 10th) to paste instantly — no arrow keys, no clicking.</li>
  <li>Fill it with your most-used text under <b>Edit Snippets</b>. It starts with a few examples you can replace.</li>
</ul>
<p>Prefer it not to auto-open? Turn it off in
<b>Preferences → General → Snippets</b>.</p>
